Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||09-14-2001||10:51 PM||||This one should be easy for some of you, but I have no experience on this....<BR>I bought some 17 inch wheels and plan on putting them on next spring... I've seen some posts saying the the inner wheelwell liner needs to be removed for these to fit or else something bad happens, but i can't find those posts anymore even when searching for them.  My question (s) is/are  1.  Do I need to remove the liner to fit these in there... and 2. If I don't what will happen?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-14-2001||11:10 PM||||What year is your Fiero? I'm running 17x7.5 .40 offset wheels on my 88 with 215/45/17 front and 245/45/17 rear tires. I haven't removed anything and nothing rubs or contacts at full lock or full suspension compression. 87's on back might have some interference with the rear strut with that tire size. 235/45/17's should clear earlier cars easily.<P>Rick <BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||09-15-2001||12:05 AM||||I had 255/40/17 rear , and 225/45/17's front with no Problem what so ever. This is with constant autocrossing and street driving. <P>Someone is feeding you some BS. Put them on ...have some fun. 1FST2m6 runs 18" wheels on his car.<P>my 17's with 45 series tires are the same height as factory 60 series tractor tires!<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black86SE||09-15-2001||12:10 AM||||I am running 17x7 5-100/4.50 American Motegi MR7 +40 with 235/45/ZR17 BFG g-force KDWS and have absolutly no problem. They are on my '86 SE. You can see what the look like on my car by the pic. There isn't any clearance problems at all.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero_3.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>1986 V6 SE<BR>Black<BR>17" Wheels<BR>P235/45/ZR17 <BR>BF Goodrich g-Force KDWS||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||09-15-2001||04:47 AM||||Someone's jealous of your new wheels  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Fieros *love* 17s, mine is a whole new car, toss 'em on and enjoy my friend!!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
